  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tree planting in Thogoto Forest  with Community Forest Association</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">During the preparations of the USB event (earlier planned for October 2024), the Food Security, Water and Climate cluster identified Thogoto Forest as an ideal site for a tree planting event. With changes to the USB timelines, the team felt it is important to proceed and support the Thogoto Community Forest to plant trees and tend for them for  a period of 6 months. The goal of the tree planting is to reiterate Netherlands commitment to conservation and collaboration with Kenya on the climate agenda. It will be an opportunity to reinforce awareness of the importance and benefit of forest conservation. The activity will support the Community Based Organization to rehabilitate a section of the forest with indigenous tree and undertake aftercare for a period of 6 months. 

USB Tree planting March 2025: It will entail  site preparation&apos;s, supporting community exhibitions, logistics and communication, tree planting and aftercare for 6 months to ensure growth  and sustainability.</narrative>
  </description>
